# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/maps/countryside_places.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event market_inn_welcome
# en: On the House
title [ff27b7] = 免费招待
# en: {The landlord of the coaching inn sets a plate in front of you that you didn't order, pie and pickles and a slab of cheese. "On the house," he beams. "We like visitors here. Always have."|The landlord again, and another plate. He asks how long you're staying, and writes the answer in a little book.|The landlord has kept you a seat by the fire. He asks after your health, your family, and whether anyone back home is expecting you soon.} {season == "winter": The fire is enormous. Nobody else sits near it.|The taproom door stands open on the green; swallows come and go under the eaves.}
text [904575] = {驿站客栈的老板把一盘你没点的菜放到你面前：馅饼、腌菜，还有一大块奶酪。“店里请的，”他满脸笑容。“我们这儿喜欢客人。一向如此。”|又是老板，又是一盘菜。他问你打算待多久，把答案记在一个小本子上。|老板在炉火边给你留了个座。他问起你的身体、你的家人，还有家里是不是有人等着你早点回去。} {season == "winter": 炉火烧得极旺。可没有别人坐在它旁边。|酒馆的门朝着草地敞开；燕子在屋檐下飞进飞出。}
# en: The warm taproom of a country coaching inn, a beaming landlord setting down a laden plate in front of a student who hasn't ordered.
scene [14230c] = 一家乡间驿站客栈温暖的酒馆里，满面笑容的老板把一盘堆得满满的菜放在一个没点菜的学生面前。
# en: Eat and thank him
opt.left.label [841fd2] = 吃了，谢谢他
# en: {It's the best pie in the valley, he says, and it might be. He watches you eat every bite.|You eat. He asks whether you've made friends in the villages yet, and seems pleased when you say not really.|You thank him. He says the thanks is all his, and means something by it you can't place.}
opt.left.say.1 [0ba8c9] = {他说这是山谷里最好的馅饼，说不定真是。他看着你吃完每一口。|你吃着。他问你在村里交到朋友没有，听你说没怎么交到，他似乎很高兴。|你谢他。他说该道谢的是他，话里有话，你却说不上是什么意思。}
# en: Insist on paying
opt.right.label [7c55b8] = 坚持付钱
# en: {He takes the coin as if it's slightly sad. It doesn't go in the till; it goes in a jar on the shelf, by itself.|You pay. He writes it in the little book, under your name, in a column that's otherwise empty.|"Your money's no good here," he says, taking it, which is the first thing he's said that you believe.}
opt.right.say.1 [2a52de] = {他收下硬币，好像有点难过。钱没有进钱柜，而是进了架子上一个单独放着的罐子。|你付了钱。他把它记进小本子，写在你名字底下，那一栏原本是空的。|“你的钱在这儿不好使，”他一边说一边收下了。这是他说的第一句你信的话。}

@event market_harvest_board
# en: The Board by the Cross
title [ba6be2] = 十字架旁的木板
# en: {Nailed to the market cross is an old board of chalked tallies, harvests by year, in columns of seven. Every year is a good one. The chalk is fresh on all of them.|The harvest board again. You count the columns this time: six full, and a seventh with this year's mark already chalked in, though the harvest isn't.|Someone has drawn a little sheaf at the top of this year's column, and a little figure beside it, very neatly.} {season == "winter": Frost has whitened the older columns; someone has wiped it off this year's.|Bees work the flowers in the trough below it.}
text [90558a] = {集市十字架上钉着一块旧木板，上面是粉笔画的计数，按年记录收成，七年一栏。每一年都是好年景。所有的粉笔印都是新的。|又是那块收成板。这回你数了数栏：六栏已满，第七栏已经用粉笔记上了今年的一道，虽然今年的收成还没到。|有人在今年那一栏的顶上画了一小束麦子，旁边还画了一个小人儿，画得很工整。} {season == "winter": 霜把旧的几栏染白了；今年那一栏的霜，有人擦掉了。|蜜蜂在下面花槽的花上忙着。}
# en: An old wooden board nailed to a market cross on a village green, covered in neat chalked tallies in seven columns, a student reading it.
scene [814768] = 村子草地上的集市十字架上钉着一块旧木板，上面是七栏整齐的粉笔计数，一个学生正在看。
# en: Copy it into your notebook
opt.left.label [51d4c9] = 抄进笔记本
# en: {You copy it all. Good, good, good, good. Nobody has a run of harvests like that. Nobody.|You copy the seventh column, mark by mark. A woman at the well watches you do it and goes indoors.|You copy the little figure. Later you notice it's wearing a coat with a long hem, like yours.}
opt.left.say.1 [87d00d] = {你全抄了下来。好，好，好，好。谁家的收成能一连好成这样。谁家都不能。|你把第七栏一道一道抄下来。井边一个女人看着你抄，转身进了屋。|你把那个小人儿也描了下来。后来你才注意到，它穿着一件下摆很长的外套，跟你的一样。}
# en: Ask someone what it counts
opt.right.label [c1a227] = 问问这是数什么的
# en: {"Good years," says a farmer. "We've been blessed." He says it like a sum he's finished.|"Harvests, dear," says a woman with a basket. "Seven good ones. We're very grateful." She doesn't say to whom.|A boy starts to tell you, and his mother calls him in mid-word.}
opt.right.say.1 [44d506] = {“好年景，”一个农夫说。“我们有福气。”他说这话的口气，像是在报一笔算完的账。|“收成呗，亲爱的，”一个挎篮子的女人说。“七个好年头。我们很感激。”她没说是感激谁。|一个男孩刚要告诉你，他妈妈就把他叫进屋了，话说了一半。}

@event market_day_stalls
# en: Everyone Smiles
title [800d8d] = 人人都在笑
# en: {Market day. Honey, wool, cheeses the size of cartwheels, and a man selling pies out of a hatbox. Everyone smiles at you. Everyone.|Market day again. The pie man has a new hatbox and the same pies.|Market day. The stallholders know your name now, though you don't remember telling it.} {season == "winter": Breath steams over the stalls; the honey is set hard.|Wasps patrol the jam.}
text [b95d9b] = {赶集日。蜂蜜、羊毛、车轮那么大的奶酪，还有一个用帽盒卖馅饼的人。每个人都冲你笑。每一个人。|又是赶集日。卖馅饼的换了个新帽盒，馅饼还是那些。|赶集日。摊主们现在都知道你的名字了，可你不记得自己告诉过谁。} {season == "winter": 摊位上方呵气成雾；蜂蜜都冻硬了。|黄蜂在果酱上巡逻。}
# en: A busy country market on a village green, stalls of honey, cheese, wool and pies, a student browsing with a basket.
scene [cfb3b1] = 村子草地上热闹的乡间集市，摊位上摆着蜂蜜、奶酪、羊毛和馅饼，一个学生提着篮子在逛。
# en: Buy something good
opt.left.label [e07940] = 买点好东西
# en: {A pot of heather honey, dark as tea. The woman won't let you leave without tasting three others.|A pie from the hatbox. It's excellent. You decide not to ask about the hatbox.|A pair of wool socks knitted, the seller says, especially for you. They fit perfectly.}
opt.left.say.1 [5fdd1e] = {一罐石楠蜜，颜色深得像茶。那女人非让你再尝三种才肯放你走。|帽盒里的一个馅饼。好吃极了。你决定不去打听那个帽盒。|一双羊毛袜，卖袜子的说，是特意为你织的。大小正合适。}
# en: Just walk the stalls
opt.right.label [c5599a] = 只逛逛摊子
# en: {You walk the whole market twice and buy nothing, and everyone is just as nice about it.|You taste everything that's offered, which is everything.|You watch the market more than shop it. Every stall has a sheaf of wheat tied over its awning.}
opt.right.say.1 [381ec0] = {你把整个集市逛了两遍，什么也没买，每个人照样待你那么好。|凡是请你尝的你都尝了，而什么都有人请你尝。|你看集市多过逛集市。每个摊位的遮棚上都系着一束麦子。}

@event market_inn_hands
# en: The Inn Wants Hands
title [3c6992] = 客栈缺人手
# en: {flag(inn_worked): The inn could use you again today, the landlord says, and he's kept your apron.|The coaching inn is short of hands, with a coach due, a yard full of barrels and a taproom to serve. "A day's wages for a day's work," says the landlord. "We look after our own."}
text [8c8097] = {flag(inn_worked): 老板说客栈今天又用得上你，还给你留着围裙。|驿站客栈人手不够：一辆马车快到了，院子里堆满了酒桶，酒馆里还得招呼客人。“干一天活，拿一天工钱，”老板说。“我们照顾自己人。”}
# en: The back door of a busy coaching inn, a harried landlord with sleeves rolled up beckoning a student towards a yard full of barrels and horses.
scene [018c32] = 一家繁忙的驿站客栈后门，卷着袖子、忙得团团转的老板招手叫一个学生到满是酒桶和马匹的院子里去。
# en: Work the day
opt.left.label [556999] = 干一天活
# en: {flag(inn_worked): Another long day. The regulars call you by name and tip you in pickles. The landlord pays you more than he said, again.|Barrels, horses, tables, plates. By evening you've carried half the valley's supper. He pays you more than he said, and won't take any back.}
opt.left.say.1 [c098c2] = {flag(inn_worked): 又是漫长的一天。常客们叫得出你的名字，拿腌菜当小费。老板付的又比说好的多。|酒桶、马匹、桌子、盘子。到傍晚，你已经端过了半个山谷的晚饭。他付的比说好的多，多出来的说什么也不肯收回。}
# en: Not today
opt.right.label [479f6f] = 今天不了
# en: {"Another day, then," he says. "There's always another day."|"Enjoy the valley," he says, and means it, and keeps looking at you after you've gone.}
opt.right.say.1 [e20a96] = {“那就改天，”他说。“总还有改天。”|“好好玩玩这山谷，”他说，是真心的。你走远了，他还在看着你。}

@event mill_skipping_rhyme
# en: Seven for the One
title [180f92] = 七，给那一位
# en: {The children on the green are skipping to a counting rhyme. One for the plough, two for the sheaf, three for the miller, on up to six. At seven they all stop, and look at whoever's nearest. Today it's you.|The rhyme again. This time you hear the words for seven, half under their breath: "and seven for the one who came."|The children start the rhyme when they see you coming, as if they've been waiting for an audience.}
text [2c9ad4] = {草地上的孩子们正跟着一首数数歌跳绳。一给犁，二给麦束，三给磨坊主，一直数到六。到了七，他们全都停下来，看着离得最近的人。今天是你。|又是那首歌。这回你听见了七的那一句，他们压低了声音：“七给那个来了的人。”|孩子们一看见你走过来就开始唱，好像一直在等观众。}
# en: Village children skipping a long rope on a green in front of a small grey chapel, chanting, one of them pointing at a passing student.
scene [218fcb] = 一座灰色小教堂前的草地上，村里的孩子们甩着长绳跳绳，边跳边唱，其中一个指着路过的学生。
# en: Learn the whole rhyme
opt.left.label [b6d29a] = 学会整首歌
# en: {A girl with a gap in her teeth teaches you the whole thing, solemnly. When you get to seven, she claps, and nobody else does.|You write it down. When you ask who "the one who came" is, the girl looks at your coat and doesn't answer.|You learn it by heart. Afterwards it goes round your head for a day, and the counting won't stop at six.}
opt.left.say.1 [6b349c] = {一个缺了颗牙的女孩一本正经地把整首教给你。你唱到七的时候，她拍手，别人谁也没拍。|你把它写下来。你问“那个来了的人”是谁，女孩看着你的外套，没有回答。|你把它背熟了。之后它在你脑子里转了一整天，数到六也停不下来。}
# en: Clap along and walk on
opt.right.label [aacc15] = 跟着拍手，然后走开
# en: {You clap along to six and leave before seven. The children wave you off, every one.|You clap. A mother calls the children in, pleasantly, as you pass.|You walk on. Behind you they start again, from one.}
opt.right.say.1 [0db858] = {你跟着拍到六，在七之前走开了。孩子们挥手送你，一个不落。|你拍着手。你经过时，一位母亲和和气气地把孩子们叫回了家。|你走开了。在你身后，他们又从一开始唱。}

@event mill_dry_wheel
# en: A Wheel With No Water
title [69f30b] = 没有水的水车
# en: {The millrace is dry tonight, mud and stones, and the wheel is turning anyway, slow and steady and wet, as if water were running over it that you can't see.|The wheel again, turning on a dry race. The miller has brought out a chair to watch it, the way you'd watch a fire.|The wheel is turning when you come, and stops when the miller sees you. He stays in his doorway, watching you watch it, and it starts again.} {season == "winter": Frost on the paddles, and still they drip.|The evening is hot and still; the wheel's breeze is cool.}
text [6cf27a] = {今晚水渠是干的，只有泥和石头，可水车照样在转，慢而稳，还湿漉漉的，就好像有你看不见的水正从它上面流过。|又是那架水车，在干水渠上转。磨坊主搬了把椅子出来看它，就像人看炉火那样。|你来的时候水车在转，磨坊主一看见你，它就停了。他站在门口，看着你看它，于是它又转了起来。} {season == "winter": 叶片上结着霜，却仍在滴水。|傍晚又热又静；水车扇起的风是凉的。}
# en: A mill at dusk, its great wheel turning slowly over an empty, dry millrace, a miller in a dusty apron watching from his door.
scene [2e4c59] = 黄昏时的磨坊，巨大的水车在一条干涸的空水渠上慢慢转着，一个系着满是面粉的围裙的磨坊主在门口看着。
# en: Ask the miller about it
opt.left.label [f583d4] = 问问磨坊主
# en: {"Turns when it likes," he says. "Always has, a good year." He offers you a sack of flour to take home, and you take it, and can't think why.|"You'll want to be indoors by dark," he says, kindly. "Valley air."|He tells you it's an old mill, and an old wheel, and an old arrangement, and then that he's said too much, though he hasn't.}
opt.left.say.1 [60bfa0] = {“它爱转就转，”他说。“好年头一向如此。”他送你一袋面粉带回去，你收下了，却想不出为什么。|“天黑前最好待在屋里，”他和气地说。“山谷里的空气。”|他告诉你这是座老磨坊，老水车，老规矩，然后说自己说得太多了，其实他并没说什么。}
# en: Watch it from the bridge
opt.right.label [29245d] = 从桥上看着
# en: {You watch until full dark. The wheel turns seven times, stops, and doesn't move again all night.|You watch. Something you can't see drips off the paddles into the dry race and doesn't wet the stones.|You time the wheel against your heartbeat. It's slower. Then it's the same.}
opt.right.say.1 [855bee] = {你一直看到天全黑。水车转了七圈，停下，一整夜再没动过。|你看着。有什么你看不见的东西从叶片上滴进干渠，却没有打湿石头。|你拿自己的心跳给水车计时。它慢一些。然后又一样了。}

@event mill_miller_sacks
# en: Sacks for the Miller
title [4a64c5] = 替磨坊主扛面粉
# en: {flag(mill_worked): The miller waves you up to the loft. He's kept the heavy sacks for you, as a compliment.|The miller needs the season's flour carted to the market village and up the hill to the farms. "Strong back?" he asks. "It pays."}
text [2b06f6] = {flag(mill_worked): 磨坊主招手叫你上阁楼。他把重的那几袋留给了你，算是一种夸奖。|磨坊主要把这一季的面粉运到集镇，再运上山坡给各家农场。“腰板结实吗？”他问。“有钱拿。”}
# en: A dusty mill loft, flour sacks stacked to the rafters, a broad miller pointing a student at a hoist and a cart waiting below.
scene [91791c] = 满是面粉的磨坊阁楼，面粉袋一直堆到房梁，一个宽肩膀的磨坊主指着吊车让学生干活，楼下停着一辆车。
# en: Cart flour all day
opt.left.label [a7a3fe] = 运一整天面粉
# en: {flag(mill_worked): Another day of flour. You're white to the elbows, your back aches, and the miller pays you in coins and a loaf that's still warm.|Sack after sack, down the hoist and onto the cart, and every farm along the road waves you in for a drink. By dusk your back has opinions. The pay is good.}
opt.left.say.1 [597d22] = {flag(mill_worked): 又是一天面粉。你从手到肘都是白的，腰也酸了，磨坊主付你钱，外加一条还热乎的面包。|一袋又一袋，从吊车上卸下来装上车，沿路每家农场都招呼你进去喝一杯。到黄昏，你的腰有了自己的意见。工钱不错。}
# en: Not today
opt.right.label [479f6f] = 今天不了
# en: {"Suit yourself," says the miller. "It'll all get carried. It always does."|He shrugs, and hoists the next sack himself.}
opt.right.say.1 [eb71b7] = {“随你，”磨坊主说。“总会有人扛的。一向如此。”|他耸耸肩，自己把下一袋吊了起来。}

@event fields_scarecrow_coats
# en: Very Decent Coats
title [2e244e] = 相当体面的外套
# en: {The scarecrows in the far field are wearing better coats than you are. Good wool, brass buttons, a travelling cloak with a stitched hem. Somebody's coats, once.|The scarecrows again. One of them has a label inside its collar, from a tailor in the capital.|There's a new scarecrow at the end of the row, in a coat that still has creases from the trunk.}
text [fd98b9] = {远处那块田里的稻草人穿的外套比你的还好。上好的羊毛，铜扣子，一件下摆缝着边的旅行斗篷。曾经是谁的外套。|又是那些稻草人。其中一个领子里缝着一枚标签，是王都一家裁缝铺的。|那一排的尽头多了一个新稻草人，身上的外套还带着在箱子里压出的褶子。}
# en: A row of scarecrows in a golden field, each dressed in a good travelling coat with brass buttons, one coat's collar turned up against no wind.
scene [d87430] = 金色田野里一排稻草人，每个都穿着一件带铜扣的好旅行外套，其中一件的领子竖着，可并没有风。
# en: Look closer at the coats
opt.left.label [19ca6e] = 凑近看看那些外套
# en: {The buttons are real brass. The pockets are empty except for one, which holds a coaching-inn ticket, years old, punched for one night only.|The tailor's label has a name stitched under it, a stranger's. You put the collar straight and don't know why that matters.|The new coat's pocket has a handkerchief in it, neatly folded. You leave it there.}
opt.left.say.1 [e3263e] = {扣子是真铜的。口袋都是空的，只有一个里面装着一张驿站客栈的票，好些年前的，打了孔，只住一晚。|裁缝的标签底下绣着一个名字，是个陌生人的。你把领子理正，却不知道这为什么要紧。|那件新外套的口袋里有一条手帕，叠得整整齐齐。你把它留在了那里。}
# en: Leave them be
opt.right.label [8e7a0b] = 别去管它们
# en: {You walk on. The scarecrows' sleeves move in the wind, all at once, all the same way.|You don't look closer. In the corner of your eye, one of them has its collar up.|You go round by the hedge. Somebody, after all, put those coats there for a reason.}
opt.right.say.1 [a0756c] = {你走开了。稻草人的袖子在风里动着，一起动，朝着同一个方向。|你没凑近看。眼角余光里，其中一个竖着领子。|你绕着树篱走。毕竟，有人把那些外套放在那儿，总有个缘故。}

@event fields_gleaners
# en: Gleaning
title [f21b36] = 拾穗
# en: {Behind the reapers, the village women glean the stray ears into their aprons, and one of them hands you a sack without asking. "Another good year," she says. "Seven, now."|The gleaners again, and the same sack. They sing as they work, the counting song the children skip to.|The gleaners make room for you in the row. "Stay for the supper," one says. "Everyone stays for the harvest supper."} The stubble crackles underfoot.
text [f36f72] = {在收割的人后面，村里的妇女们把散落的麦穗拾进围裙，其中一个二话不说递给你一只口袋。“又是个好年头，”她说。“七个了。”|又是那些拾穗的人，又是那只口袋。她们边干活边唱，唱的正是孩子们跳绳时的那首数数歌。|拾穗的人在行里给你让出位置。“留下来吃晚饭吧，”一个人说。“丰收晚宴，人人都留下来。”} 麦茬在脚下噼啪作响。
# en: Village women in aprons gleaning stray ears of grain behind the reapers in a golden field, one of them handing a student a sack.
scene [eee8f7] = 金色田野里，系着围裙的村妇跟在收割的人后面拾散落的麦穗，其中一个正把口袋递给一个学生。
# en: Glean with them
opt.left.label [cdbfc8] = 跟她们一起拾
# en: {Your back aches and your sack is pitiful and they praise it extravagantly.|You glean until the light goes. They walk you to the lane, all of them, chatting, as if you might get lost.|You glean and listen. Nobody says what comes after seven. They just call this one "the good one".}
opt.left.say.1 [4d8fb1] = {你腰酸背痛，口袋里少得可怜，她们却夸得天花乱坠。|你一直拾到天色暗下来。她们全都陪你走到小路口，说说笑笑，好像怕你迷路。|你一边拾一边听。没人说七以后是什么。她们只管今年叫“好年”。}
# en: Ask about the harvest supper
opt.right.label [c39af0] = 问问丰收晚宴的事
# en: {"Oh, you'll come," she says. "Visitors are the guests of honour. It's tradition." Everyone near enough to hear nods.|"At the inn, end of the season," she says. "The landlord does the honours." She looks at your coat when she says it.|They tell you about the supper: the long table, the sheaf, the toast to the guest. Nobody tells you whose turn it is to be the guest.}
opt.right.say.1 [43ca37] = {“哦，你会来的，”她说。“客人是贵宾。这是老传统。”离得够近听得见的人都点了点头。|“在客栈，季末的时候，”她说。“由老板主持。”她说这话时看着你的外套。|她们给你讲晚宴：长桌、麦束、向客人敬的酒。没人告诉你今年轮到谁当那位客人。}

@event fields_harvest_day
# en: Harvest Hands
title [5fb9f8] = 收割帮工
# en: {season == "winter": {flag(fields_worked): The farmer has a billhook waiting for you again.|Even in winter there's work, hedges to lay and ditches to clear. {at_home(): A neighbour you've known all your life|A farmer at the gate} holds out a billhook. "Day's wages," he says.}|{flag(fields_worked): The farmer has a scythe waiting for you again, and your name on the wages list.|The farmers are a hand short in the long field, and {at_home(): the neighbour who taught you to tie a sheaf|a farmer at the gate} holds out a scythe. "Day's wages, and supper," he says.}}
text [cf38b1] = {season == "winter": {flag(fields_worked): 那位农夫又给你备好了一把柴刀。|就算是冬天也有活干：编树篱、清水沟。{at_home(): 一位你从小就认识的邻居|一个站在田门口的农夫}递过来一把柴刀。“一天的工钱，”他说。}|{flag(fields_worked): 那位农夫又给你备好了一把镰刀，工钱单上也写着你的名字。|长田里少一个人手，{at_home(): 当年教你捆麦束的那位邻居|一个站在田门口的农夫}递过来一把镰刀。“一天的工钱，管晚饭，”他说。}}
# en: A farmer at a field gate under a huge sky holding out a tool to a student, farmhands at work in the field behind.
scene [7fcbe6] = 辽阔天空下，一个农夫站在田门口，把一件农具递给一个学生，身后的田里有雇工在干活。
# en: Work the day in the field
opt.left.label [c6b5c3] = 在田里干一天
# en: {season == "winter": {flag(fields_worked): Another day of mud and thorns, hands raw, and good pay for it.|Hedges laid, ditches cleared, hands raw. The farmer pays you and says you're a natural, which you aren't.}|{flag(fields_worked): Another day's harvest. They save you the end of the row, where the last sheaf stands, and nobody will cut it but you.|All day in the long rows. You're the slowest in the line and they cheer every sheaf you tie. The pay is good; the supper is better.}}
opt.left.say.1 [55cfaf] = {season == "winter": {flag(fields_worked): 又是一天泥水和荆棘，手都磨破了，工钱不错。|树篱编好了，水沟清干净了，手也磨破了。农夫付你钱，说你是天生干这个的，其实你不是。}|{flag(fields_worked): 又是一天收割。他们把这一行的尽头留给你，最后一束麦子立在那里，除了你谁也不肯割。|在长长的麦垄里干了一整天。你是这一排最慢的，你每捆好一束他们都欢呼。工钱不错，晚饭更好。}}
# en: Not today
opt.right.label [479f6f] = 今天不了
# en: {season == "winter": {"Another day," says the farmer, cheerfully.|He shrugs, and lays the hedge himself.}|{"Another day," says the farmer, cheerfully. "The last sheaf'll wait for you."|He shrugs and swings the scythe himself.}}
opt.right.say.1 [a6c4a8] = {season == "winter": {“改天吧，”农夫高高兴兴地说。|他耸耸肩，自己编起了树篱。}|{“改天吧，”农夫高高兴兴地说。“最后那一束会等着你的。”|他耸耸肩，自己挥起了镰刀。}}

@event ridge_count_aloud
# en: Counting Out Loud
title [678f48] = 大声数
# en: {A shepherd on the ridge path tells you not to count the stones out loud, which is exactly the kind of advice that makes you want to.|The stones again. You count them in your head and get nineteen, the same as everyone gets.|The ring of stones. Somebody has tied red thread round one of them, knotted seven times.}
text [516cde] = {山脊小路上一个牧羊人叫你别把石头大声数出来，而这正是那种让人偏想去做的忠告。|又是那些石头。你在心里数了数，十九块，和大家数的一样。|那一圈石头。有人在其中一块上系了红线，打了七个结。}
# en: A student walking the inside of a ring of leaning standing stones on a bare ridge, touching each stone, lips moving, the valley far below.
scene [962c3c] = 光秃的山脊上，一个学生沿着一圈倾斜的立石内侧走着，摸着每一块石头，嘴唇在动，山谷远在下方。
# en: Count them aloud
opt.left.label [e71ae1] = 大声数出来
# en: {"Seventeen, eighteen, nineteen." You turn. "Twenty." There were nineteen. You count again in silence, and get nineteen.|You count aloud and get twenty, and the wind drops completely until you've walked out of the ring.|You count aloud, and at twenty a sheep in the valley below stops grazing and looks up at the ridge.}
opt.left.say.1 [f613d8] = {“十七，十八，十九。”你转过身。“二十。”明明是十九块。你默默再数一遍，十九。|你大声数，数到二十，风一下子全停了，直到你走出那个圈。|你大声数，数到二十时，下面山谷里一只羊停下吃草，抬头望向山脊。}
# en: Count in your head and leave it
opt.right.label [ca82eb] = 在心里数，然后算了
# en: {Nineteen, in your head. The stones lean a little, as if listening for the number.|Nineteen. You keep it to yourself. The wind keeps blowing, which feels like approval.|You don't count at all today. You just touch the threaded stone, and it's warm, and the others are cold.}
opt.right.say.1 [0266e6] = {十九，在心里。石头微微倾着，像在听那个数。|十九。你没说出口。风照样吹着，像是一种赞许。|你今天一块也没数。你只摸了摸那块系着线的石头，它是暖的，别的都是凉的。}

@event ridge_night_sky
# en: Sightlines
title [837485] = 视线
# en: {At night you notice what the stones on the ridge are for. Each gap between two of them frames a piece of the valley rim, and a star rises in some of them, exactly.|Another clear night at the stones. {flag(ridge_chart): You've started a chart of which gap catches which star.|You pick out which gap catches which star, and wish you'd brought paper.}|The stones at night again. Tonight a star is rising in a gap {flag(ridge_chart): where, by your chart, there should be nothing.|that framed nothing at all the last time you looked.}} {season == "winter": Frost on the stones; the stars are hard and close.|Warm grass, moths, and the sky turning slowly over the ring.}
text [dfd281] = {夜里你才看出山脊上那些石头是做什么用的。每两块石头之间的缝隙都框住一段山谷的边沿，有些缝里会不偏不倚地升起一颗星。|又一个晴朗的夜晚，又在石头边。{flag(ridge_chart): 你已经开始画一张图，记下哪道缝接住哪颗星。|你辨认着哪道缝接住哪颗星，后悔没带纸来。}|夜里又来到石头边。今晚有一颗星正从一道缝里升起，{flag(ridge_chart): 而照你的图，那里本该什么也没有。|而上回你看的时候，那道缝里什么也没框住。}} {season == "winter": 石头上结着霜；星星又硬又近。|温暖的草，飞蛾，天空在石圈上方缓缓旋转。}
# en: A student kneeling at a gap between two leaning standing stones on a dark ridge, sighting along it at a bright star rising over the valley rim.
scene [e8ae32] = 漆黑的山脊上，一个学生跪在两块倾斜的立石之间的缝隙前，顺着它瞄向山谷边沿上升起的一颗亮星。
# en: Chart the sightlines till dawn
opt.left.label [1f33ef] = 画视线图，直到天亮
# en: {You sight along the gaps until the cold gets into your knees. Whoever raised these stones knew the sky better than half the astronomy faculty.|You chart the gaps by lantern. One frames nothing at all, no star, all year; you mark it with a question.|You stay till dawn. The new star sets in the gap that framed nothing, and the valley goes quiet, every dog and every cockerel, until the sun is up.}
opt.left.say.1 [d9236f] = {你顺着一道道缝瞄过去，直到寒气钻进膝盖。立起这些石头的人，比天文系一半的教员都更懂天空。|你借着提灯把那些缝画下来。有一道什么也框不住，一整年都没有星；你在它旁边画了个问号。|你待到天亮。那颗新星落进了那道什么也框不住的缝里，山谷一下子安静了，每一条狗、每一只公鸡，直到太阳升起。}
# en: Come down before midnight
opt.right.label [9f7ffe] = 午夜前下山
# en: {You come down by the shepherd's path with the stars on your shoulders. A good night.|You come down early. The lane lamps of both villages are lit, every one, as if for a guest.|You come down before the cold sets in, and sleep better for it.}
opt.right.say.1 [e8d488] = {你沿着牧羊人的小路下山，星星落在你肩上。一个好夜晚。|你早早下了山。两个村子小巷里的灯全都亮着，一盏不落，像是在等一位客人。|你在寒气上来之前下了山，睡得也更好。}
